      "title": "Incorrect Token Address for NoCapLimit Override",
      "uid": "3AxUq2FDg3j",
      "updatedAt": "2025-11-03T08:56:10.802Z",
      "user": {
        "uid": "URs2NJv6trA",
        "handle": "Petrus"
      },
      "sensitivity": "non-sensitive",
      "aiSeverity": null,
      "aiValidity": null,
      "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\n \nThe issue is in the LatentSwapLEX.sol, \n \n```solidity \n/** \n\n * @title Latent Swap LEX \n\n * @author Covenant Labs \n\n **/ \n\n \n\n/** \n\n * @dev Emitted when default noCapLimit is set for a token \n\n * @param token the token address \n\n * @param oldDefaultNoCapLimit the old default noCapLimit for markets with this quote token \n\n * @param newDefaultNoCapLimit the new default noCapLimit for markets with this quote token \n\n **/ \n\n@> event SetDefaultNoCapLimit(address indexed token, uint8  oldDefaultNoCapLimit, uint8 newDefaultNoCapLimit); \n\n@> event SetMarketNoCapLimit(MarketId indexed marketId, uint8 oldNoCapLimit, uint8 newNoCapLimit); \n\n \n\ncontract LatentSwapLEX is ILatentSwapLEX, TokenData, Ownable2Step { \n\n``` \n\nThe tokenNoCapLimit mapping is intended for quote tokens (as per the event comment: \"for markets with this quote token\"). \n \nHowevere,  in the function initMarket, \n```solidity \nfunction initMarket( MarketId marketId, MarketParams calldata marketParams, uint32 protocolFee, bytes calldata initData ) external onlyCovenantCore returns (SynthTokens memory synthTokens, bytes memory lexData) { if (lexConfig[marketId].aToken != address(0)) revert LSErrors.E_LEX_AlreadyInitialized(); \n\nLatentSwapLogic.MarketInitInfo memory info = LatentSwapLogic.getInitMarketInfo( \n   marketParams, \n   _debtDuration, \n   _edgeSqrtPriceX96_A, \n   _edgeSqrtPriceX96_B, \n@>   tokenNoCapLimit[marketParams.baseToken],  // <-- BUG: Uses baseToken instead of quoteToken \n   _assetDecimals(marketParams.quoteToken), \n   _assetSymbol(marketParams.quoteToken) \n); \n \n// ... (rest of function continues ) \n \n\n} \n\n``` \nIt passes marketParams.baseToken (the collateral asset, e.g., ETH) instead of marketParams.quoteToken (the stable asset, e.g., USDT). This means default noCapLimit overrides set via setDefaultNoCapLimit (which takes a quote token address) will be ignored, and markets will fall back to an unintended (or zero) value based on the base token. Therefore, the code incorrectly passes marketParams.baseToken as the key to fetch this default, so new markets inherit the wrong cap limit (e.g., from the base token's override, or fallback to 1 if none exists), ignoring the intended quote-token-specific configuration. \n\n## Impact  \nThis issue causes newly initialized markets to apply incorrect default mint/redeem cap limits based on the base token instead of the quote token, potentially leading to overly restrictive or permissive operations that disrupt expected collateralization and trading behavior.  Meaning New markets will use incorrect noCapLimit values (e.g., defaulting to 0, meaning 1 baseToken cap), leading to unexpected mint/redeem behavior or DoS on initialization. \n \n\n \n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\n\n\nChange the fetch in initMarket to use marketParams.quoteToken instead of marketParams.baseToken to align with the comment's intent for quote-token overrides, ensuring correct default noCapLimit application without affecting existing markets. \n\nFixed Code \n\n```solidity \n\nLatentSwapLogic.MarketInitInfo memory info = LatentSwapLogic.getInitMarketInfo( \n   marketParams, \n   _debtDuration, \n   _edgeSqrtPriceX96_A, \n   _edgeSqrtPriceX96_B, \n   tokenNoCapLimit[marketParams.quoteToken],  // Fixed: Use quoteToken for overrides \n   _assetDecimals(marketParams.quoteToken), \n   _assetSymbol(marketParams.quoteToken) \n); \n\n```",
      "proofOfConcept": "## POC \nCreate a new test file, run with; forge test --match-test test_NoCapLimit_Bug_QuoteTokenVsBaseToken --via-ir -vvvv \n\n \n \n \n```solidity \n// SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later \n\npragma solidity ^0.8.30; \n\n \n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\"; \n\nimport {LatentSwapLEX} from \"../src/lex/latentswap/LatentSwapLEX.sol\"; \n\nimport {MarketParams, MarketId} from \"../src/interfaces/ICovenant.sol\"; \n\nimport {FixedPoint} from \"../src/lex/latentswap/libraries/FixedPoint.sol\"; \n\nimport {MockERC20} from \"./mocks/MockERC20.sol\"; \n\nimport {MockOracle} from \"./mocks/MockOracle.sol\"; \n\nimport {LexConfig} from \"../src/lex/latentswap/interfaces/ILatentSwapLEX.sol\"; \n\n \n\ncontract NoCapLimitBugTest is Test { \n\n    // Price constants for LEX initialization \n\n    uint160 constant P_MAX = uint160((1095445 * FixedPoint.Q96) / 1000000); \n\n    uint160 constant P_MIN = uint160(FixedPoint.Q192 / P_MAX); \n\n    uint160 P_LIM_H = uint160((P_MAX * 9500) / 10000); \n\n    uint160 P_LIM_MAX = uint160((P_MAX * 9999) / 10000); \n\n    uint32 constant DURATION = 30 * 24 * 60 * 60; \n\n    uint8 constant SWAP_FEE = 0; \n\n    int64 constant LN_RATE_BIAS = 5012540000000000; \n\n \n\n    LatentSwapLEX latentSwapLEX; \n\n    address mockOracle; \n\n    address usdtToken; \n\n    address ethToken; \n\n    address btcToken; \n\n \n\n    function setUp() public { \n\n        // Deploy oracle \n\n        mockOracle = address(new MockOracle(address(this))); \n\n \n\n        // Deploy quote token (USDT) - this should have a default noCapLimit set \n\n        usdtToken = address(new MockERC20(address(this), \"USDT\", \"USDT\", 6)); \n\n \n\n        // Deploy two different base tokens \n\n        ethToken = address(new MockERC20(address(this), \"Ethereum\", \"ETH\", 18)); \n\n        btcToken = address(new MockERC20(address(this), \"Bitcoin\", \"BTC\", 8)); \n\n \n\n        // Deploy LEX with standard parameters \n\n        latentSwapLEX = new LatentSwapLEX( \n\n            address(this), \n\n            address(this), \n\n            P_MAX, \n\n            P_MIN, \n\n            P_LIM_H, \n\n            P_LIM_MAX, \n\n            LN_RATE_BIAS, \n\n            DURATION, \n\n            SWAP_FEE \n\n        ); \n\n    } \n\n \n\n    function test_NoCapLimit_Bug_QuoteTokenVsBaseToken() public { \n\n        // INTENT: Demonstrate that setDefaultNoCapLimit intends to set the cap for QUOTE TOKENS, \n\n        // but the code incorrectly uses BASE TOKENS when initializing markets. \n\n \n\n        // Setup: Set a specific noCapLimit for USDT (quote token)  \n\n        // This should mean all markets using USDT as quote should get this noCapLimit \n\n        uint8 expectedNoCapLimitForUSDT = 25; \n\n        latentSwapLEX.setDefaultNoCapLimit(usdtToken, expectedNoCapLimitForUSDT); \n\n \n\n        // Create first market: ETH/USDT \n\n        // Expected behavior: Should use the USDT quote token's default noCapLimit (25) \n\n        // Actual buggy behavior: Will look up ETH base token's default instead \n\n        MarketParams memory ethUsdtParams = MarketParams({ \n\n            baseToken: ethToken, \n\n            quoteToken: usdtToken, \n\n            curator: mockOracle, \n\n            lex: address(latentSwapLEX) \n\n        }); \n\n \n\n        MarketId ethUsdtMarketId = MarketId.wrap( \n\n            bytes20(uint160(uint256(keccak256(abi.encode(ethUsdtParams))))) \n\n        ); \n\n \n\n        latentSwapLEX.initMarket(ethUsdtMarketId, ethUsdtParams, 0, hex\"\"); \n\n \n\n        // Create second market: BTC/USDT \n\n        // Expected behavior: Should also use the USDT quote token's default noCapLimit (25) \n\n        // Actual buggy behavior: Will look up BTC base token's default instead \n\n        MarketParams memory btcUsdtParams = MarketParams({ \n\n            baseToken: btcToken, \n\n            quoteToken: usdtToken, \n\n            curator: mockOracle, \n\n            lex: address(latentSwapLEX) \n\n        }); \n\n \n\n        MarketId btcUsdtMarketId = MarketId.wrap( \n\n            bytes20(uint160(uint256(keccak256(abi.encode(btcUsdtParams))))) \n\n        ); \n\n \n\n        latentSwapLEX.initMarket(btcUsdtMarketId, btcUsdtParams, 0, hex\"\"); \n\n \n\n        // Get the noCapLimit for both markets \n\n        LexConfig memory ethUsdtConfig = latentSwapLEX.getLexConfig(ethUsdtMarketId); \n\n        LexConfig memory btcUsdtConfig = latentSwapLEX.getLexConfig(btcUsdtMarketId); \n\n \n\n        // ISSUE DEMONSTRATION: \n\n        // Both markets have the SAME quote token (USDT) which has a set default of 25 \n\n        // Therefore, both markets SHOULD have noCapLimit = 25 \n\n \n\n        // However, due to the bug: \n\n        // - ETH/USDT market gets noCapLimit based on ethToken's default (not set, falls back to 60) \n\n        // - BTC/USDT market gets noCapLimit based on btcToken's default (not set, falls back to 60) \n\n        // While this happens to result in same value, it's using WRONG TOKEN for lookup \n\n \n\n        // Now set a specific value for one base token to show the real impact \n\n        uint8 customNoCapForETH = 15; \n\n        latentSwapLEX.setDefaultNoCapLimit(ethToken, customNoCapForETH); \n\n \n\n        // Create a new ETH/USDT market \n\n        MarketParams memory ethUsdt2Params = MarketParams({ \n\n            baseToken: ethToken, \n\n            quoteToken: usdtToken, \n\n            curator: mockOracle, \n\n            lex: address(latentSwapLEX) \n\n        }); \n\n \n\n        MarketId ethUsdt2MarketId = MarketId.wrap( \n\n            bytes20(uint160(uint256(keccak256(abi.encode(ethUsdt2Params, \"v2\"))))) \n\n        ); \n\n \n\n        latentSwapLEX.initMarket(ethUsdt2MarketId, ethUsdt2Params, 0, hex\"\"); \n\n        LexConfig memory ethUsdt2Config = latentSwapLEX.getLexConfig(ethUsdt2MarketId); \n\n \n\n        // PROOF OF BUG: \n\n        // This new ETH/USDT market will use ETH's noCapLimit (15) instead of USDT's (25) \n\n        // because the code looks up tokenNoCapLimit[marketParams.baseToken] instead of [marketParams.quoteToken] \n\n \n\n        // The bug is proven when: \n\n        // 1. ETH/USDT (with ETH override) has noCapLimit = 15 (using base token) \n\n        // 2. BTC/USDT (without base token override) has noCapLimit = 60 (using base token default) \n\n        // 3. Both should have noCapLimit = 25 (the USDT quote token's configured value) \n\n \n\n        assertEq( \n\n            ethUsdt2Config.noCapLimit, \n\n            customNoCapForETH, \n\n            \"BUG CONFIRMED: Market uses base token (ETH) noCapLimit instead of quote token (USDT)\" \n\n        ); \n\n \n\n        // This proves the code incorrectly passes marketParams.baseToken to fetch default \n\n        // when it should pass marketParams.quoteToken \n\n        assertNotEq( \n\n            ethUsdt2Config.noCapLimit, \n\n            expectedNoCapLimitForUSDT, \n\n            \"Market should have used quote token (USDT) default noCapLimit, not base token (ETH)\" \n\n        ); \n\n    } \n\n} \n\n```",
